This product includes software developed by third parties. The Go module graph
in go.mod pins exact versions; this file names what is compiled into the
released binaries and the licence each one carries.

The CLI and server archives bundle:

- minio/selfupdate (https://github.com/minio/selfupdate), used by `eznit
  update` and the window's About panel.
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0; the text is in LICENSE-APACHE.

The archives that carry the desktop app (the CLI archives) bundle the Fyne
toolkit and its dependencies:

- Fyne (https://fyne.io), licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License; the text is
  in LICENSE-FYNE.
- Fyne systray (https://github.com/fyne-io/systray), licensed under the
  Apache License, Version 2.0; the text is in LICENSE-APACHE.
- go-gl/gl and go-gl/glfw (https://github.com/go-gl), the OpenGL bindings and
  the GLFW windowing library. go-gl is BSD 3-Clause; GLFW is zlib.
- go-text/typesetting and go-text/render (https://github.com/go-text),
  licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
- srwiley/oksvg and srwiley/rasterx (https://github.com/srwiley), the SVG and
  raster backends, licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.
- nfnt/resize (https://github.com/nfnt/resize), licensed under the ISC
  License.
- golang.org/x/image, golang.org/x/text and golang.org/x/sys
  (https://golang.org/x), licensed under the BSD 3-Clause License.

The full licence text of each module travels in the Go module cache and in the
module's own repository; the three texts required to accompany a binary
distribution are included in this folder: LICENSE (this project, MIT),
LICENSE-FYNE (BSD 3-Clause) and LICENSE-APACHE (Apache 2.0).
